# Testing (Vitest)

## Purpose

Make behavior verifiable and regressions cheap to catch, using one testing style across the
monorepo.

## Why it exists

CI runs `pnpm test` on every push/PR to `main` ([ci.yml](mdc:.github/workflows/ci.yml)), and
Turbo runs `test` after `^build` + `check-types` ([turbo.json](mdc:turbo.json)). Tests are the
contract for watcher/store/adapter/handler behavior.

## Layout & naming

- Tests live in each package's `tests/` folder. Core mirrors `src/` (e.g.
  `src/watchers/cache_watcher.ts` -> `tests/watchers/cache_watcher.test.ts`). Handlers use a
  flat `tests/` with one file per tool (`prisma.test.ts`, `nodemailer.test.ts`).
- Name files `*.test.ts`. Run with `pnpm test` (per package: `vitest run`).

## Conventions

- Import explicitly from `vitest`: `describe`, `it`, `expect`, `vi`, `beforeEach`, `Mock` — do
  not rely on globals in core/handlers.
- Nest `describe` for the unit and each method; write behavior-focused `it("should ...")` names.
- Reset state in `beforeEach(() => vi.clearAllMocks())`; restore timers/spies in `afterEach`.
- Never hit a real database, filesystem, network, or clock.

## Mocking the store & context

Mock the store by extending the abstract `Store` with `vi.fn()` members, and mock the context
module so `getStore()` returns it — see
[request_watcher.test.ts](mdc:packages/core/tests/watchers/request_watcher.test.ts):

```typescript
class MockStore extends Store {
  initialize = vi.fn();
  save = vi.fn();
  // ...all abstract members as vi.fn()
}
vi.mock("../../src/context/context", () => ({ getStore: vi.fn() }));
```

Assert on the EXACT persisted payload (including normalized/redacted fields):

```typescript
expect(mockStore.save).toHaveBeenCalledWith({
  id: "request-1",
  type: WatcherTypeEnum.REQUEST,
  minimal_data: { /* ... */ },
  data: { /* headers lowercased, secrets "*******" */ },
});
```

## Testing handlers (event/hook based)

Mock the workspace boundaries (`vi.mock("@lensjs/core", ...)`, `vi.mock("@lensjs/date", ...)`
for deterministic time, `vi.mock("../src/utils/emitter", ...)`), run the factory, then CAPTURE
the registered listener and invoke it to simulate an event:

```typescript
const listener = prismaMock.$on.mock.calls[0][1];
await listener(event);
expect(onQueryMock).toHaveBeenCalledWith({ query, duration, createdAt, type });
```

Test pure helpers (e.g. `normalizeSql`, `sequelizeEventHandler`, `buildMimeParts`) in isolated
`describe` blocks; use `it.each([...])` for table-driven cases; use `vi.useFakeTimers()` +
`vi.setSystemTime(...)` when a handler stamps its own time.

## Requirement

Add or update tests for ANY bug fix or new behavior in `@lensjs/core`, adapters, and handlers.
A behavior change without a test change should not merge.

## AI must never

- Introduce a test that depends on a real DB/network/clock, or on wall-clock time.
- Assert with loose matchers when the exact payload is knowable.
- Ship a behavior change in a watcher/store/adapter/handler without a corresponding test.
